Question 2: Shopping Mall Billing Management System
Write a C program to develop a Shopping Mall Billing Management System using Call by Value. A customer purchases the following products:
•	Laptop: ₹50,000
•	Smartphone: ₹20,000
•	Headphones: ₹3,000
•	Keyboard: ₹2,000
The program should perform the following operations using separate functions:
1.	Calculate the total price of all products.
2.	Calculate a 10% discount on the total price.
3.	Calculate GST at 18% on the discounted price.
4.	Calculate the final payable amount.
5.	Calculate the average price of the purchased products.
6.	Display the original prices of all products after calculations.
All functions must receive values using Call by Value. Original product prices must remain unchanged.

products = {
    "Laptop": 50000,
    "Smartphone": 20000,
    "Headphone": 3000,
    "Keyboard": 2000,
}


def calculate_total_price(items):
    return sum(items.values())


def calculate_discount(total):
    return total * 0.10


def calculate_GST(discount_price):
    return discount_price * 0.18


def calculate_final_amount(discount_price, gst):
    return discount_price + gst


def calculate_avg_price(items):
    return sum(items.values()) / len(items)


def display(items):
    total = calculate_total_price(items)
    discount = calculate_discount(total)
    discount_price = total - discount
    gst = calculate_GST(discount_price)
    final_amount = calculate_final_amount(discount_price, gst)
    avg_price = calculate_avg_price(items)

    print("Total Price:", total)
    print("Discount (10%):", discount)
    print("Price After Discount:", discount_price)
    print("GST (18%):", gst)
    print("Final Payable Amount:", final_amount)
    print("Average Price:", avg_price)

    print("\nOriginal Product Prices:")
    for product, price in items.items():
        print(product, ":", price)
