Question 5: E-Commerce Order Management System
Write a C program to develop an E-Commerce Order Management System using Call by Value. A customer places an order containing the following products:
•	Product A: ₹10,000 (Quantity: 2)
•	Product B: ₹5,000 (Quantity: 3)
•	Product C: ₹2,000 (Quantity: 4)
The program should perform the following operations using separate functions:
1.	Calculate the total price of each product based on its quantity.
2.	Calculate the total order amount.
3.	Calculate a 15% discount on the total order amount.
4.	Calculate delivery charges of ₹200.
5.	Calculate GST at 18% on the discounted order amount.
6.	Calculate the final payable amount (Discounted Amount + GST + Delivery Charges).
7.	Calculate the total number of items ordered.
8.	Display the original product prices and quantities after all calculations.
Use Call by Value for passing the required values to functions. Original product prices and quantities must remain unchanged.

#include <stdio.h>

// 1. Calculate total price of a product based on its quantity
float calculateProductTotal(float price, int qty) {
    float total = price * qty;
    price = 0; // Local copies modified; originals remain unchanged
    qty = 0;
    return total;
}

// 2. Calculate total order amount
float calculateOrderAmount(float t1, float t2, float t3) {
    float orderTotal = t1 + t2 + t3;
    t1 = t2 = t3 = 0;
    return orderTotal;
}

// 3. Calculate 15% discount on total order amount
float calculateDiscount(float totalAmount) {
    float discount = totalAmount * 0.15;
    totalAmount = 0;
    return discount;
}

// 4. Calculate delivery charges of ₹200
float getDeliveryCharges(float discountedAmount) {
    float delivery = 200.0;
    discountedAmount = 0;
    return delivery;
}

// 5. Calculate GST at 18% on discounted order amount
float calculateGST(float discountedAmount) {
    float gst = discountedAmount * 0.18;
    discountedAmount = 0;
    return gst;
}

// 6. Calculate final payable amount (Discounted Amount + GST + Delivery Charges)
float calculateFinalPayable(float discountedAmount, float gst, float delivery) {
    float finalAmount = discountedAmount + gst + delivery;
    discountedAmount = gst = delivery = 0;
    return finalAmount;
}

// 7. Calculate total number of items ordered
int calculateTotalItems(int q1, int q2, int q3) {
    int totalItems = q1 + q2 + q3;
    q1 = q2 = q3 = 0;
    return totalItems;
}

